# apps/api/Dockerfile.dockerignore — BuildKit uses THIS file (not the root
# .dockerignore) whenever the api image is built with `-f apps/api/Dockerfile`;
# it replaces the root list, so it carries a full copy plus the api-only
# excludes. `apps/web` and `docs` used to sit in the root file, which also
# removed apps/web from the WEB image's context (docker-web: "docker-entrypoint.sh
# not found", 2026-08-29). Keep the shared part in sync with /.dockerignore.

# Python
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

# Node
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Build outputs
**/.next/*
**/dist
**/build
**/out
.nx

# Docker
infra/docker/data

# Git
.git

# IDE
.idea
.vscode
*.swp

# Misc
.DS_Store
*.log
coverage
.nyc_output
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

**/test-results
**/.turbo
# Anchored AND nested: a bare `__pycache__` only matches at the context root, so
# libs/shared/py/__pycache__/*.pyc (rewritten by every test lane, different
# bytes per workspace) rode into the `libs` bind mount of the uv sync layer and
# re-keyed it on every runner change — measured 2026-08-28: 48-72 s uv sync +
# ~3 min of dependent layers on an app-only change.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.venv

# Not inputs of the api image; keeps the cold build context small.
apps/web
docs
